The class KernelFunctionFromPrompt is internal and the method CaptureUsageDetails is private, so we cannot subclass or call it directly in tests outside the assembly. Also, the interface IChatCompletionService or ITextCompletion used in the snippet is not found or accessible.

Given these constraints, I will write a minimal test that verifies the ILogger.LogWarning call by creating a minimal internal test class inside the same namespace and using reflection to invoke the private method CaptureUsageDetails. This will allow us to test the logging behavior without needing to subclass or access internal types directly.

